    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=085269": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Geography",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/11/2026 Assistant Professor in Geography Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Assistant Professor in Geography JOB SYNOPSIS The School of History and Geography invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor in Physical Geography. UL Geography is a dynamic and interdisciplinary group of academics, with research strengths including population and migration, humanitarian entrepreneurship, climate and environmental change, digital and spatial humanities, cultural and historical geography, river management and conservation, natural hazards and risk management, geospatial data science, and urban ecosystem services. Our staff have secured national, EU, and international funding, and contribute to impactful research addressing major societal challenges. We seek to appoint a scholar with expertise in physical geography who will strengthen the discipline’s research profile and deliver high quality, research-led teaching in the areas of geoinformatics, remote sensing, computational modelling, machine learning, and/or landscape assessment. The successful candidate will join a collegial and ambitious school committed to excellence in scholarship, teaching, and societal engagement. The appointee will be required to compete for national and international research funding aligned with their area of expertise and the Faculty of Arts, Humanities and Social Sciences Research Funding Themes. Faculty of Arts, Humanities & Social Sciences School of History and Geography Contract Type: Permanent Salary Scale: €49,424 - €67,221 p.a. University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Professor Alistair Malcolm Head School of History and Geography University of Limerick Email: alistair.malcolm@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Wednesday, 18th November 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Academic Contact Email : Job ID : 085269 Contact Number : Close Date : 18-Nov-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=085131": {
      "title": "Chief Technical Officer - PESS",
      "description": "Closing Date: 13/11/2026 Chief Technical Officer - PESS Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Chief Technical Officer - PESS JOB SYNOPSIS The Department of Physical Education and Sport Sciences is seeking to appoint an experienced and dynamic Chief Technical Officer (CTO) on a full-time basis to lead and manage the Department’s technical operations in support of its teaching, research, and performance activities. This senior role is central to ensuring the safe functioning of all laboratory and technical facilities. The CTO will provide leadership and oversight of the Department’s technical services, managing and developing a team of technical staff to deliver high-quality support across a broad range of academic, research, and engagement activities. Key responsibilities include the management of technical infrastructure, coordination of laboratory and field-based technical support, implementation and monitoring of health and safety procedures, and collaboration with academic, research, and professional services staff to support the Department’s evolving needs and priorities. The successful candidate will possess substantial experience in managing technical operations within a sport sciences or related environment, together with a strong understanding of laboratory and performance testing facilities, equipment maintenance, regulatory compliance, and health and safety standards. Excellent organisational, communication, and team leadership skills are essential. Faculty of Education & Health Sciences Department of Physical Education & Sport Science Contract Type: Permanent Salary Scale: €68,138 - €82,623 p.a. University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Dr John L Perry Head Department of Physical Education & Sport Science University of Limerick Email: PESSHoD@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Friday, 13th November 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Are you currently legally entitled to work and reside in Ireland? If you are not currently an EEA Citizen and have stated that you are currently legally entitled to work and reside in Ireland, you MUST upload a copy of your current Visa and Work permit in the attachments section application form. Unfortunately, if the attachment, as noted, is required and not provided your application cannot be processed. Please note your current work authorisation status must allow you to fulfil the terms of the contract on offer. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Staff Contact Email : Job ID : 085131 Contact Number : Close Date : 13-Nov-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=085230": {
      "title": "Cloud Architect – Governance & Architecture Specialist",
      "description": "Closing Date: 03/12/2026 Cloud Architect – Governance & Architecture Specialist Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Cloud Architect – Governance & Architecture Specialist JOB SYNOPSIS The Cloud Architect, Governance & Architecture Specialist is a key member of the Enterprise Architecture team within the University of Limerick's Information Technology Division. The role is responsible for shaping and enabling the secure, compliant and strategic adoption of cloud, AI and enterprise technologies across the University. The post holder will develop practical governance frameworks, architecture patterns and technical controls that support secure, compliant and innovative technology adoption. Working across a diverse university community, the role will provide technical leadership and expert advice on enterprise platforms, helping to ensure technology investments align with institutional objectives, regulatory requirements and best practice. Office of the Director of Information Technology Information Technology Division Contract Type: Permanent Salary Scale: €70,551- €113,366 p.a. University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Ms Treasa Cunneen Head of Enterprise Architecture Information Technology Division University of Limerick Email: treasa.cunneen@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Thursday, 3rd December 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Are you currently legally entitled to work and reside in Ireland? If you are not currently an EEA Citizen and have stated that you are currently legally entitled to work and reside in Ireland, you MUST upload a copy of your current Visa and Work permit in the attachments section application form. Unfortunately, if the attachment, as noted, is required and not provided your application cannot be processed. Please note your current work authorisation status must allow you to fulfil the terms of the contract on offer. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Staff Contact Email : Job ID : 085230 Contact Number : Close Date : 03-Dec-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=085289": {
      "title": "Cyber Security Architect",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/11/2026 Cyber Security Architect Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Cyber Security Architect JOB SYNOPSIS We are seeking an experienced Cyber Security Architect to design, develop and implement robust security architectures that protect the organisation’s systems, networks, applications and data. The role is responsible for defining security standards, identifying and mitigating cyber risks, and ensuring security is embedded across technology projects and business operations. Office of the Director of Information Technology Information Technology Division Contract Type: Permanent Salary Scale: €70,551 - €113,366 p.a. University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Mr Bob Loftus Head of Cyber Security Information Technology Division University of Limerick Email: bob.loftus@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Monday, 30th November 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Are you currently legally entitled to work and reside in Ireland? If you are not currently an EEA Citizen and have stated that you are currently legally entitled to work and reside in Ireland, you MUST upload a copy of your current Visa and Work permit in the attachments section application form. Unfortunately, if the attachment, as noted, is required and not provided your application cannot be processed. Please note your current work authorisation status must allow you to fulfil the terms of the contract on offer. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Staff Contact Email : Job ID : 085289 Contact Number : Close Date : 30-Nov-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
