    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=085110": {
      "title": "Digital Spaces Facilitator - Glucksman Library Makerspace",
      "description": "Closing Date: 06/11/2026 Digital Spaces Facilitator - Glucksman Library Makerspace Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Digital Spaces Facilitator - Glucksman Library Makerspace JOB SYNOPSIS The Library Digital Spaces Facilitator offers a structured professional development opportunity for individuals seeking to gain experience in creative technologies, digital media, and innovation-focused learning environments. As a key member of the Glucksman Library team, the post supports the operation and development of The Edge, the Library's technology-rich hub for making, creating, and digital production. The role contributes to the library’s mission of enabling creativity, innovation, digital skills development, and technology-enhanced learning across the University of Limerick community. The Glucksman Library serves UL students, staff, researchers, and academic staff through a range of study, learning, and specialist digital creation environments. These include The Edge, home to the library’s makerspace, Equipment Lending Service, and media production facilities, which support active learning, inclusive teaching practices, digital scholarship, and collaborative project work. Aligned with UL's Learning, Teaching and Assessment Strategy, these spaces foster creativity, problem-solving, experimentation, and student success. Working within a supportive and collaborative team environment, the Digital Spaces Facilitator provides frontline support, training, and guidance to users while contributing to the ongoing delivery and enhancement of innovative library services. The role combines operational service delivery with professional development, providing opportunities to develop expertise in digital fabrication, maker technologies, media production, technology-enhanced learning, and user engagement within a vibrant academic setting. Office of the Provost & Deputy President Library & Information Services Division Contract Type: Fixed Term (23 Months) Salary Scale: €35,906 - €48,244 p.a. pro rata University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Ms Louise O'Shea Learning Spaces Manager Library & Information Services Division University of Limerick Email: louise.oshea@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Friday, 6th November 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Are you currently legally entitled to work and reside in Ireland? If you are not currently an EEA Citizen and have stated that you are currently legally entitled to work and reside in Ireland, you MUST upload a copy of your current Visa and Work permit in the attachments section application form. Unfortunately, if the attachment, as noted, is required and not provided your application cannot be processed. Please note your current work authorisation status must allow you to fulfil the terms of the contract on offer. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Staff Contact Email : Job ID : 085110 Contact Number : Close Date : 06-Nov-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=085251": {
      "title": "EMERGE Implementation Officer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/11/2026 EMERGE Implementation Officer Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: EMERGE Implementation Officer JOB SYNOPSIS The EMERGE Implementation Officer is a senior operational coordination role supporting the University of Limerick’s participation in the EMERGE European University Alliance under the Erasmus+ European Universities Initiative. Reporting to the EMERGE Project Manager, the postholder will act as the principal local operational coordination point for EMERGE activities within UL. The role will support the administration and institutional implementation of Alliance activities across governance, reporting, communications, stakeholder engagement and operational follow-up. The post holder will coordinate activities involving academic departments, professional service units, governance structures and international university partners. The role also includes the day-to-day operational coordination and supervision of the EMERGE support team within a matrix management environment, balancing UL-focused implementation requirements with Alliance-wide and WP1 operational support activities. The successful candidate will require strong organisational capability, stakeholder management skills and operational judgement, together with the ability to coordinate multiple concurrent workstreams and respond effectively to evolving institutional and Alliance priorities. The role will contribute significantly to the effective implementation of EMERGE within UL while supporting wider Alliance objectives and maintaining alignment with university strategy, governance and operational requirements. Office, VP Global & Community Engagement Global & Community Engagement Contract Type: Specific Purpose Salary Scale: €61,642 - €87,643 p.a. pro rata University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Mr John Mulcahy EMERGE Project Manager Global & Community Engagement University of Limerick Email: john.mulcahy@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Thursday, 12th November 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Are you currently legally entitled to work and reside in Ireland? If you are not currently an EEA Citizen and have stated that you are currently legally entitled to work and reside in Ireland, you MUST upload a copy of your current Visa and Work permit in the attachments section application form. Unfortunately, if the attachment, as noted, is required and not provided your application cannot be processed. Please note your current work authorisation status must allow you to fulfil the terms of the contract on offer. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Staff Contact Email : Job ID : 085251 Contact Number : Close Date : 12-Nov-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
