    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=085253": {
      "title": "Psychologist Assistant (formerly Assistant Psychologist)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/11/2026 Psychologist Assistant (formerly Assistant Psychologist) Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Psychologist Assistant (formerly Assistant Psychologist) JOB SYNOPSIS The psychology assistant will report to the Head of Counselling (a clinical psychologist) and work within a team of psychotherapists and other psychology assistants. Key elements of the role will be to roll out step 1 of the primary care model by engaging in psychological screening and risk-assessment, as well as providing 1:1 psychoeducational support to students. Wider service elements of the role will include working on clinically relevant service-based projects, supporting and facilitating group work, and contributing to projects, committees, and representation of the counselling service within the Division of Student Affairs. Office of the Provost & Deputy President Student Affairs Division Contract Type: 1 Year Fixed Term Salary Scale: €42,220 - €55,976 p.a. University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Dr Lucy Smith Head of Counselling University of Limerick Email: lucy.smith@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Thursday, 5th November 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. This position is subject to Garda Vetting and Foreign Police Clearance. If you have resided outside Ireland for a cumulative period of 36 months or more over the age of 18 years you must furnish a Foreign Police Clearance (FPC) from the country or countries of residence. Please note; any costs incurred in this process will be borne by the candidate. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties If you are not currently an EEA Citizen and have stated that you are currently legally entitled to work and reside in Ireland, you MUST upload a copy of your current Visa and Work permit in the attachments section application form. Unfortunately, if the attachment, as noted, is required and not provided your application cannot be processed. Please note your current work authorisation status must allow you to fulfil the terms of the contract on offer. Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Staff Contact Email : Job ID : 085253 Contact Number : Close Date : 05-Nov-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=085249": {
      "title": "Research Funding Officer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 17/11/2026 Research Funding Officer Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Research Funding Officer JOB SYNOPSIS Join the University of Limerick's Research Office and play a key role in supporting the University's ambitious research strategy. As part of the Research Support Services (RSS) team, the Research Funding Officer will work closely with researchers to identify, develop and secure competitive national, European and international research funding opportunities. The role has a particular focus on EU programmes, including Horizon Europe and the European Research Council (ERC), and involves supporting the preparation, submission and administration of high-quality funding applications. This is an exciting opportunity for a motivated professional with strong organisational, project management and communication skills to contribute to the growth of UL's research excellence and international research profile. Office of the VP Research Contract Type: Specific Purpose Salary Scale: €61,642 - €87,643 p.a. pro rata University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Dr Imelda Doolan Research Support Officer, EU and International Funding team lead Office of the VP Research University of Limerick Email: imelda.doolan@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Tuesday, 17th November 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Are you currently legally entitled to work and reside in Ireland? If you are not currently an EEA Citizen and have stated that you are currently legally entitled to work and reside in Ireland, you MUST upload a copy of your current Visa and Work permit in the attachments section application form. Unfortunately, if the attachment, as noted, is required and not provided your application cannot be processed. Please note your current work authorisation status must allow you to fulfil the terms of the contract on offer. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Staff Contact Email : Job ID : 085249 Contact Number : Close Date : 17-Nov-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
