    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=085329": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Computational Mechanics",
      "description": "Closing Date: 16/11/2026 Assistant Professor in Computational Mechanics Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Assistant Professor in Computational Mechanics JOB SYNOPSIS If you are seeking an academic career in an inspiring and cohesive Engineering School that delivers excellence in research, teaching, innovation, and societal impact, then the permanent position of Assistant Professor in Computational Mechanics within the School of Engineering at the University of Limerick may be of interest to you. The School of Engineering has established strengths in mechanical engineering, materials engineering, composites, manufacturing, biomedical engineering, fluid dynamics, digital engineering, and computational modelling, supported by strong links with national and international industry partners and world-class research infrastructure. The school is committed to conducting impactful research that addresses major societal and industrial challenges through engineering innovation. The successful candidate will have a primary degree in Mechanical Engineering, Civil Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, Applied Mathematics, Computational Engineering, or a closely related discipline, together with a PhD (Level 10 NFQ) in Computational Mechanics or a closely related field. The successful candidate will be expected to establish an internationally recognised independent research programme supported by competitive external funding and to supervise postgraduate research students. The candidate will contribute to multidisciplinary research activities within the School of Engineering and associated research Institutes/centres such as the Bernal Institute and other relevant research groupings across the University. Candidates should demonstrate the ability to deliver high-quality teaching in Computational Mechanics and related engineering topics and be committed to excellence in teaching, student learning, and curriculum development. Faculty of Science & Engineering School of Engineering Contract Type: Permanent Salary Scale: €49,424 - €67,221 p.a. University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Professor David Newport Head School of Engineering University of Limerick Email: david.newport@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Monday, 16th November 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Academic Contact Email : Job ID : 085329 Contact Number : Close Date : 16-Nov-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=085330": {
      "title": "Clinical Tutor in Clinical and Communication Skills",
      "description": "Closing Date: 13/11/2026 Clinical Tutor in Clinical and Communication Skills Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Clinical Tutor in Clinical and Communication Skills JOB SYNOPSIS The Clinical Tutor in Clinical and Communication Skills will play a key role in designing, delivering, and developing modules on Clinical and Communication Skills for the Direct Entry Medicine Programme (DEM), with a key emphasis on professional values. A significant responsibility of the role will be leadership of the Very Early Patient Contact Programme of the DEM, ensuring high-quality early clinical learning experiences for students and maintaining strong partnerships with healthcare providers. They will support student learning through teaching, mentoring, curriculum development, assessment, and educational quality assurance, while promoting professionalism, communication, and clinical competence. The role requires substantial experience in clinical and professional skills education, particularly in small-group teaching and supporting diverse student cohorts. The successful candidate will work collaboratively across multidisciplinary teams to deliver an integrated and student-centred curriculum. They will also contribute to educational research, scholarship, quality improvement, and the wider strategic and academic activities of the Medical School. Faculty of Education & Health Sciences School of Medicine Contract Type: Permanent Salary Scale: €69,835 - €82,235 p.a. University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Dr Lisa Moran School of Medicine University of Limerick Email: lisa.moran@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Friday, 13th November 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Academic Contact Email : Job ID : 085330 Contact Number : Close Date : 13-Nov-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=085349": {
      "title": "Student Volunteer Ireland Project Manager (0.6FTE)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/11/2026 Student Volunteer Ireland Project Manager (0.6FTE) Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Student Volunteer Ireland Project Manager (0.6FTE) JOB SYNOPSIS Student Volunteer Ireland (SVI) is a collaboration of seven (soon to be 12) higher education institutions (HEIs) that provides the infrastructure (technical system and resourcing) for www.StudentVolunteer.ie (SV.ie) a one-stop portal connecting students with Volunteer Involving Organisations (VIOs) and volunteering opportunities. SVI is hosted by the University of Limerick on behalf of its members. SV.ie is a bespoke, state-of-the-art IT management system that tracks, records, and reports on higher education student volunteering, and skills obtained. It enables clubs, societies, and community organisations, both on and off campus, to promote their volunteer opportunities to students. Student Volunteer Ireland is recruiting an ambitious Project Manager to lead on the development and implementation of Phase Two of its work programme which involves continuing to grow and embed SV.ie across the higher education sector, researching its impact at national level and developing sustainable infrastructure and operating models beyond 2029. The role will be based at the University of Limerick on behalf of Student Volunteer Ireland. Office of the Provost & Deputy President Student Affairs Division Contract Type: Specific Purpose Salary Scale: €70,551 - €113,366 p.a. pro rata University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Dr Rhona McCormack Director of Student Affairs University of Limerick Email: rhona.mccormack@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Wednesday, 18th November 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Are you currently legally entitled to work and reside in Ireland? If you are not currently an EEA Citizen and have stated that you are currently legally entitled to work and reside in Ireland, you MUST upload a copy of your current Visa and Work permit in the attachments section application form. Unfortunately, if the attachment, as noted, is required and not provided your application cannot be processed. Please note your current work authorisation status must allow you to fulfil the terms of the contract on offer. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Staff Contact Email : Job ID : 085349 Contact Number : Close Date : 18-Nov-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=085369": {
      "title": "Technical Services Manager - Buildings and Estates",
      "description": "Closing Date: 04/12/2026 Technical Services Manager - Buildings and Estates Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Technical Services Manager - Buildings and Estates JOB SYNOPSIS The University of Limerick is seeking an experienced Technical Services Manager to provide leadership across the University’s mechanical, electrical and building services infrastructure and support the continued development of a world-class campus environment. Reporting to the Head of Technical Services and Sustainability, the role is responsible for the operational governance, resilience and lifecycle management of critical infrastructure systems across a large and diverse estate. The successful candidate will lead technical services operations, infrastructure renewal programmes, contractor and service provider performance, statutory compliance, asset management and technical support for capital projects. As a senior member of the Technical Services and Sustainability Team, the Technical Services Manager will contribute to strategic estate planning, infrastructure investment decisions, operational excellence and the delivery of long-term sustainability objectives. The role offers the opportunity to influence the future development of a growing and increasingly complex university estate while leading a highly skilled technical function. This position will appeal to an experienced engineering professional with strong technical, leadership and stakeholder management capabilities who is seeking a challenging and rewarding management role within higher education. Office of the Director of Buildings and Estates Buildings and Estates Department Contract Type: Permanent Salary Scale: €70,551 - €113,366 p.a. University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Mr Eric Crowe Head of Technical Services and Sustainability Buildings and Estates Department University of Limerick Email: eric.crowe@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Friday, 4th December 2026. Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Are you currently legally entitled to work and reside in Ireland? If you are not currently an EEA Citizen and have stated that you are currently legally entitled to work and reside in Ireland, you MUST upload a copy of your current Visa and Work permit in the attachments section application form. Unfortunately, if the attachment, as noted, is required and not provided your application cannot be processed. Please note your current work authorisation status must allow you to fulfil the terms of the contract on offer. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Staff Contact Email : Job ID : 085369 Contact Number : Close Date : 04-Dec-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    }
  },
